checks_run.procedure:
My own contract-generated sweep over every P5 operation (p5-operations.ts: 194 operations, 90 mutations, 40 transformation-scoped reads), as a disposable integration test.

The callers:
- AUD (org A) sends every P5 mutation;
- ADM_ACCESS+ADM_TECH (org A) sends every mutation and every transformation-scoped read;
- an ADM_METHOD-only user sends every transformation-scoped read and write.

Each request uses a real transformation id, If-Match "1", an Idempotency-Key and the declared media type. Each response's status, problem pointers and audit actions are recorded.

The sweep ran four times:
1. run 1: synthetic code params;
2. run 2: well-formed code params;
3. run 3: well-formed bodies for the writes that validate the body before authorization;
4. run 4 (final): run 3 plus a non-empty inputValues body.

Navigation is hidden server-side (identity/navigation.ts: hidden areas are omitted, `holdsAnywhere`).

Read the P5 diff (e70ac02..270ebbf, 881 files) for every P5 mutation's five properties (commit-time re-authorization, validation, If-Match, one audit event, no remote I/O in the transaction). I concentrated on these:
- exports (create, list, download, cancel);
- Studio review SoD (API and the 0062/0097 triggers);
- approvals (routes, routedApproverOf, approver_configured, admin approvers);
- procedures (Rule A in 0096, authorizeStepWrite in D-167);
- attachments and bulk edit (IDOR, locking);
- automation identity, human-only actions and the dry run;
- demo isolation and the dev-issuer binding;
- self-grant.
The notes with file:line are in 50-source-review.md.

Review migrations 0062-0097:
- ordering and gaps;
- row guards and version steps;
- grants (no DELETE);
- append-only history;
- snapshot immutability;
- 0094's one-off trigger disable (ADR-0039 C2);
- 0096's narrowed guard.
Then reproduce the runner's ordering behaviour with its own compareStatus() for a later file in a P5 gap.

checks_run.actual:
Formula injection holds:
- user text with a trigger character is quote-prefixed in CSV;
- in XLSX it is always an inline string, never <f> (sheet.ts:3-7);
- the only formula is SUM(<col><first>:<col><last>) built from integers, emitted only when every cell is a number and the decimal.js sum equals the total (model.ts totalRowCells);
- the forms CSV leaves only DECIMAL-matching values unprefixed.

No float: the Number() uses in the diff are versions, cursors, counts and integer rubric levels. Money, rates, NPV and ROI use decimal.js (finance/metrics.ts at precision 40, rounded once).

Defect F-DG5-101 (Low, non-mandatory): a decimal with more than 15 significant digits becomes a text cell (model.ts:191, :206), and csv.ts:48 re-neutralizes it. So -12345678901.23456 and -1234567890.123456 are written '-12345678901.23456 and '-1234567890.123456. The control (15 significant digits) and the positive long value are unprefixed. 43-csv-long-decimal.log has 1 failed and 2 passed, exit 1: the failure is exactly that assertion, by design. XLSX is unaffected.
